		stem: 'All ISMS documents live in a wiki that anyone can edit, with no version history and no approval record. Which requirement is most directly failed?',
		options: ['Clause 7.5.3, because documented information is not adequately controlled for version, approval and protection from alteration', 'Clause 7.4, because the organization has not determined how ISMS information is communicated internally', 'Clause 5.2, because the information security policy cannot be shown to have been formally approved', 'Clause 9.2, because audit evidence cannot be relied upon when the underlying documents are mutable'],
		correct_option: 'A',
		explanation: 'Clause 7.5.3 requires control over distribution, access, retrieval, version and protection from unintended alteration. An open wiki fails on version control regardless of content quality.',
